We'll go as far as we can.

14:49:31.685 --> 14:49:32.819
Marriott World Trade Center.

14:49:32.886 --> 14:49:33.520
Where are they trapped,

14:49:33.520 --> 14:49:33.553
K?

14:49:33.553 --> 14:49:36.056
What do you call the urgent?

14:49:36.056 --> 14:49:40.794
Supported to be in a fell area.

14:49:40.794 --> 14:49:41.594
Unicorn urgent.

14:49:41.594 --> 14:49:43.296
We're in that two world trade center.

14:49:43.296 --> 14:49:44.964
We have some of the individuals in the front.

14:49:45.231 --> 14:49:46.333
We're waiting to evacuate them,

14:49:46.333 --> 14:49:46.433
K.

14:49:46.533 --> 14:49:48.635
10-4,

14:49:48.668 --> 14:49:49.369
also be advised,

14:49:49.369 --> 14:49:51.037
in a fell area at the Marriott Hotel.

14:49:51.638 --> 14:49:53.807
Receiving reports of firefighters trapped and down.

14:49:53.807 --> 14:49:54.507
Yeah,

14:49:54.507 --> 14:49:55.342
I'll go back.

14:50:11.291 --> 14:50:11.424
What

14:50:11.424 --> 14:50:11.825
are you looking at?

14:50:11.825 --> 14:50:15.562
10-4. I think it was my family to make sure they knew I was okay because they know that I work here.

14:50:18.832 --> 14:50:21.201
It just tore me up, like it tore up the building.

14:50:23.203 --> 14:50:25.739
And I just can't believe anyone could do that,

14:50:26.906 --> 14:50:28.742
regardless of what your political views are.

14:50:47.026 --> 14:50:47.761
Is closed down.

14:50:47.794 --> 14:50:49.062
Let's go back to Lauren Ashburn,

14:50:49.129 --> 14:50:51.464
who's in the USA today. Building in Roslyn.

14:50:51.531 --> 14:50:51.765
Lauren?

14:50:52.265 --> 14:50:52.465
Yes,

14:50:52.532 --> 14:50:52.999
good morning,

14:50:53.066 --> 14:50:53.800
Buck and Andrea.

14:50:53.933 --> 14:50:56.236
I am taking a look right now at the Pentagon.

14:50:56.669 --> 14:50:57.404
There are one,

14:50:57.570 --> 14:50:57.837
two,

14:50:58.204 --> 14:50:58.538
three,

14:50:58.838 --> 14:51:01.808
four helicopters I can see from the vista here.

14:51:01.975 --> 14:51:07.414
The USA Today Tower 1 building that overlooks all of Washington from Arlington,

14:51:07.480 --> 14:51:07.914
Virginia.

14:51:08.581 --> 14:51:10.617
I can see one helicopter is on its way,

14:51:10.617 --> 14:51:11.618
it looks like to me,

14:51:11.785 --> 14:51:13.520
to the Washington Hospital Center.

14:51:13.586 --> 14:51:15.422
It's attempting a landing right now.

14:51:16.556 --> 14:51:16.823
I'm sure.

14:51:16.856 --> 14:51:20.527
Sure, there are two others following in that direction at this point.

14:51:21.027 --> 14:51:22.195
I'm looking down at traffic.

14:51:22.228 --> 14:51:25.298
Traffic is at a standstill leaving the city.

14:51:25.698 --> 14:51:26.900
Can I ask you a real quick question?

14:51:27.333 --> 14:51:28.435
Just what are they telling you?

14:51:28.468 --> 14:51:29.602
Like, what are you supposed to do?

14:51:29.669 --> 14:51:30.203
What's the plan?

14:51:31.838 --> 14:51:32.205
What's that?

14:51:32.205 --> 14:51:37.210
I mean, just not even in terms of what happened, but I'm just trying to figure out what they're talking about.

14:52:00.200 --> 14:52:01.301
I'm standing outside St.

14:52:01.367 --> 14:52:04.604
Vincent's hospital right now, where the scene is absolutely unbelievable.

14:52:04.704 --> 14:52:05.672
When I arrived here,

14:52:06.773 --> 14:52:10.443
it was just as the second building explosion happened.

14:52:10.610 --> 14:52:14.647
And there is what I could describe as chaos in the streets here.

14:52:14.714 --> 14:52:17.484
There are hundreds of people just in shock,

14:52:18.017 --> 14:52:20.186
police officers telling people to go home,

14:52:20.487 --> 14:52:22.288
obviously worried about crowd control.

14:52:22.956 --> 14:52:24.023
But at the hospital,

14:52:24.357 --> 14:52:27.760
there has not been much activity in terms of ambulances arriving here,

14:52:27.827 --> 14:52:29.596
though you might expect there would.

14:52:29.662 --> 14:52:36.970
Be after that last explosion, some hospital, some ambulances took off and headed down

14:52:37.370 --> 14:52:40.673
Seventh Avenue, which is otherwise closed to traffic, but st.

14:52:40.707 --> 14:52:54.721
Vincent is obviously preparing for the possibility of many, many people arriving at their emergency room. They have what looks like a trauma center set up on the street, on the sidewalk of Seventh Avenue.

14:53:10.837 --> 14:53:10.970
Well,

14:53:11.037 --> 14:53:11.237
Erin,

14:53:11.905 --> 14:53:12.772
I'm in our bureau,

14:53:12.939 --> 14:53:14.541
but I have on the telephone with me

14:53:14.908 --> 14:53:21.080
Barbara, who is the wife of a friend of mine. And who is an eyewitness to exactly what happened at the Pentagon.

14:53:21.247 --> 14:53:21.548
Barbara,

14:53:22.248 --> 14:53:23.182
can you hear me all, right?

14:53:23.383 --> 14:53:23.550
Yes,

14:53:23.583 --> 14:53:24.083
I can hear you.

14:53:24.450 --> 14:53:24.584
Well,

14:53:24.584 --> 14:53:25.952
what exactly did you see?

14:53:26.486 --> 14:53:33.860
Let's look at the Pentagon now, as you describe what exactly happened at the Pentagon this morning.

14:53:34.127 --> 14:53:36.563
As we were driving into town on 395,

14:53:36.763 --> 14:53:37.530
there was an exit.

14:53:37.764 --> 14:53:39.866
We were trying to get off the exit for the Memorial Bridge.

14:53:40.466 --> 14:53:46.506
Off to the left-hand side was a commercial plane that came in and was coming too fast and too low.

14:53:46.940 --> 14:53:50.043
And the next thing we saw was it go down below the side of the road,

14:53:50.577 --> 14:53:52.178
and we just saw the fire.

14:53:53.580 --> 14:53:54.547
That came up after that.

14:53:54.847 --> 14:53:56.082
How large was the explosion?

14:53:56.783 --> 14:53:57.450
It was large.

14:53:58.217 --> 14:53:59.385
Was there sound as well?

14:54:01.020 --> 14:54:03.656
That I can't verify because windows were up in the vehicle.

14:54:04.891 --> 14:54:06.192
Was it clear to you what had happened?

14:54:06.593 --> 14:54:06.826
Yes,

14:54:07.160 --> 14:54:07.594
definitely.

14:54:08.294 --> 14:54:12.565
So you believe it was a commercial airliner that was hitting the Pentagon?

14:54:13.232 --> 14:54:13.499
Yes,

14:54:13.900 --> 14:54:18.538
and I'm not sure exactly where the Pentagon was in relationship to where the plane went down.

14:54:19.939 --> 14:54:21.708
But they are relatively close to one another.

14:54:21.774 --> 14:54:23.576
Whether it hit any part of that Pentagon,

14:54:23.610 --> 14:54:24.177
I'm not sure.

14:54:25.144 --> 14:54:26.179
How low was the plane?

14:54:26.846 --> 14:54:27.780
When it was coming down?

14:54:27.947 --> 14:54:28.081
Yeah.

14:54:28.881 --> 14:54:32.418
It was coming down on less than a

14:54:32.785 --> 14:54:39.692
45-degree angle and coming down to the side of the 395.

14:54:40.426 --> 14:54:41.260
And when it came down,

14:54:41.294 --> 14:54:43.796
it just missed the 395 and went down below it,

14:54:43.863 --> 14:54:47.066
and then you saw the fire come up from it.

14:54:47.233 --> 14:54:50.570
Were you able to see what kind of plane or what airline it belonged to?

14:54:50.870 --> 14:54:51.004
No,

14:54:51.037 --> 14:54:52.605
I did not see what kind of an airline.

14:54:52.639 --> 14:54:56.142
I just assumed because we were so close to the airport, it was coming into land.

14:54:57.276 --> 14:54:58.444
But it seemed awfully low to you?

14:54:58.578 --> 14:54:58.845
Yes,

14:54:59.445 --> 14:54:59.946
and fast.

14:55:00.713 --> 14:55:01.748
How big was the fireball?

14:55:05.551 --> 14:55:07.954
I was spatially challenged at times and it was pretty big.

14:55:08.921 --> 14:55:09.889
What did you think was happening?

14:55:10.590 --> 14:55:14.293
I know that that hit the ground and exploded.

14:55:15.328 --> 14:55:16.562
Were you frightened yourself?

14:55:16.829 --> 14:55:17.096
Yes,

14:55:17.664 --> 14:55:17.830
yes,

14:55:17.897 --> 14:55:20.533
everybody stopped the cars and we all got out of it and so forth.

14:55:22.101 --> 14:55:22.301
Right,

14:55:22.301 --> 14:55:22.402
well,

14:55:22.435 --> 14:55:23.236
thank you very much.

14:55:23.436 --> 14:55:23.736
Thank you.

14:55:23.736 --> 14:55:24.637
Appreciate your talking to us.

14:55:24.737 --> 14:55:24.937
Erin,

14:55:25.004 --> 14:55:25.438
back to you.

14:55:25.805 --> 14:55:26.072
David,

14:55:26.139 --> 14:55:26.539
Thank you.

14:55:41.888 --> 14:55:42.955
What we're looking at,

14:55:43.256 --> 14:55:43.756
spin around,

14:55:43.756 --> 14:55:44.724
we can see the picture from,

14:55:44.791 --> 14:55:45.925
this is from where we're standing.

14:55:46.225 --> 14:55:49.962
We're a good 20 blocks or more from the World Trade Center as we're standing here.

14:55:49.962 --> 14:55:50.997
And you can see the flames,

14:55:51.497 --> 14:55:52.532
you see where the hole is.

14:55:52.699 --> 14:55:53.766
And you can see how the hole,

14:55:53.766 --> 14:55:54.701
the original hole is,

14:55:54.734 --> 14:55:55.868
which is in the middle of the building.

14:55:56.169 --> 14:55:57.003
And if you look at it,

14:55:57.136 --> 14:55:58.438
you can see how the hole has grown.

14:55:58.604 --> 14:55:59.672
Also, the flames below,

14:56:00.106 --> 14:56:01.407
maybe 10 floors below now,

14:56:01.774 --> 14:56:03.843
those flames have spread from the original fire.

14:56:04.110 --> 14:56:05.211
We've seen with binoculars,

14:56:05.211 --> 14:56:06.679
there have been people out here with binoculars.

14:56:07.046 --> 14:56:08.381
They've seen people in the buildings.

14:56:08.381 --> 14:56:13.252
There are still people in that tower.

14:56:13.753 --> 14:56:14.687
Screaming through the air.

14:56:15.121 --> 14:56:16.856
Anybody could do that to innocent people.

14:56:18.791 --> 14:56:20.927
I remember looking at the clock that it was 9 o'clock.

14:56:21.327 --> 14:56:21.761
And I said,

14:56:21.828 --> 14:56:25.865
here's people sitting at their desks with families.

14:56:27.033 --> 14:56:28.067
And then they weren't anymore.

14:56:31.370 --> 14:56:33.005
Then there was a second plane.

14:56:33.339 --> 14:56:34.507
Then I was on the phone with my mother,

14:56:34.841 --> 14:56:36.509
looking out my window in my office,

14:56:37.477 --> 14:56:38.010
and she said,

14:56:38.111 --> 14:56:38.611
Oh my god,

14:56:38.678 --> 14:56:39.512
Another plane hit,

14:56:39.612 --> 14:56:41.547
and then I saw the burst of flames,

14:56:42.415 --> 14:56:43.149
and the smoke,

14:56:44.050 --> 14:56:45.151
and I just started screaming.

14:56:46.486 --> 14:56:47.987
Because then I felt it all over again.

14:56:49.589 --> 14:56:50.790
I just felt it all over again.

14:57:12.612 --> 14:57:12.845
Um,

14:57:13.412 --> 14:57:13.546
John,

14:57:13.579 --> 14:57:14.614
before I come back to you,

14:57:14.680 --> 14:57:16.315
Dennis Cross is on the phone.

14:57:16.349 --> 14:57:16.582
Dennis,

14:57:16.582 --> 14:57:16.949
do you hear me?

14:57:18.484 --> 14:57:19.118
Dennis Cross,

14:57:19.118 --> 14:57:19.519
Do you hear me?

14:57:19.519 --> 14:57:20.019
Yes,

14:57:20.019 --> 14:57:20.119
I can,

14:57:20.119 --> 14:57:20.253
Peter.

14:57:20.520 --> 14:57:20.787
Dennis,

14:57:20.820 --> 14:57:26.359
I understand that you were in the World Trade Center when either this or these attacks occurred.

14:57:26.459 --> 14:57:26.893
Am I correct?

14:57:26.893 --> 14:57:27.026
Yeah,

14:57:27.093 --> 14:57:27.560
that's correct.

14:57:27.560 --> 14:57:27.693
It was,

14:57:27.693 --> 14:57:27.794
uh,

14:57:27.994 --> 14:57:31.264
I guess it was slightly before 9 o'clock,

14:57:31.264 --> 14:57:31.364
and,

14:57:31.364 --> 14:57:31.464
uh,

14:57:31.531 --> 14:57:33.332
I work on the 36th floor in one World Trade Center.

14:57:33.332 --> 14:57:35.301
I work for in the insurance industry,

14:57:36.502 --> 14:57:42.208
probably hundreds of people in my industry in both of these two buildings.

14:57:43.142 --> 14:57:44.343
And what happened?

14:57:45.178 --> 14:57:46.245
As I was...

14:57:46.245 --> 14:57:46.512
Dennis,

14:57:46.546 --> 14:57:47.613
just let me stop for a second.

14:57:48.781 --> 14:57:50.783
Somebody is trying another telephone on this line.

14:57:50.783 --> 14:57:52.385
Could they please not do that while we listen to Mr.

14:57:52.418 --> 14:57:52.718
Cross?

14:57:52.752 --> 14:57:52.985
Thanks.

14:57:52.985 --> 14:57:53.286
Go ahead,

14:57:53.286 --> 14:57:53.419
Mr.

14:57:53.452 --> 14:57:53.686
Cross.

14:57:55.454 --> 14:57:56.022
Go ahead,

14:57:56.055 --> 14:57:56.255
Dennis.

14:57:56.289 --> 14:57:56.756
Essentially,

14:57:56.856 --> 14:57:59.258
I was at my desk working,

14:57:59.992 --> 14:58:00.960
general office activity,

14:58:01.093 --> 14:58:02.295
and felt an enormous...

14:58:04.630 --> 14:58:05.832
It almost felt like an earthquake.

14:58:05.865 --> 14:58:10.303
I could literally feel and see things in the office moving and the floor moving.

14:58:11.404 --> 14:58:15.341
Immediately after it was some sort of explosion or something,

14:58:16.576 --> 14:58:19.512
there was an enormous volume of debris and paper.

14:58:19.512 --> 14:58:21.747
It almost looked like a dirty parade.

14:58:22.615 --> 14:58:24.350
All of this material just falling down.

14:58:24.684 --> 14:58:28.287
I was looking out the south side of the

14:58:29.021 --> 14:58:32.825
One World Trade, and everybody in the office was kind of screaming,

14:58:32.925 --> 14:58:35.161
kind of gathering in the middle. And I went to the window and

14:58:36.362 --> 14:58:39.632
I immediately saw one woman, who appeared to be a woman.

14:58:39.665 --> 14:58:41.667
Appeared to be motionless,

14:58:41.701 --> 14:58:45.204
laying on the roof of a lower building next to me.

14:58:45.204 --> 14:58:46.939
At that point,

14:58:46.973 --> 14:58:48.474
everybody started to gather their things.

14:58:48.507 --> 14:58:52.311
They were trying to evacuate people down the stairwell.

14:58:52.411 --> 14:58:53.779
Did the electricity go out in the building?

14:58:54.580 --> 14:58:55.348
The tower was a little bit closer to the TOWER.

14:58:55.348 --> 14:58:55.781
I thought it was a TOWER.

14:58:55.781 --> 14:58:57.416
The lights flickered a couple of times and then it was WEIRD.

14:58:57.416 --> 14:58:58.818
It was kind of like there was

14:59:00.386 --> 14:59:01.153
one sort of rush,

14:59:02.088 --> 14:59:02.455
and then

14:59:03.489 --> 14:59:05.091
surely after that there was another ONE.

14:59:05.091 --> 14:59:05.925
I don't know if it was

14:59:06.459 --> 14:59:08.694
maybe the other tower, or if there were

14:59:09.262 --> 14:59:10.429
elevators in the inside of IT,

14:59:10.429 --> 14:59:11.330
you KNOW,

14:59:11.631 --> 14:59:13.666
sort of just dropping to the FLOOR.

14:59:13.733 --> 14:59:14.500
Are you aware that

14:59:15.001 --> 14:59:17.370
one of the twin tray towers has now collapsed on ITSELF?

14:59:23.576 --> 14:59:24.410
Looked at it on the screen.

14:59:24.410 --> 14:59:40.059
Screen here, Dennis. We could see the smoke from this collapse. Just sweep the billow forward through the lower blocks of Manhattan. Did you have a sense of that completely? I was at that point. I'm a little bit northwest, it's certainly north, maybe to the west side of

14:59:41.294 --> 14:59:50.169
Tower one, and I was trying to get to Broadway. My wife works on the other side of downtown, here, I'm still trying to get there. But the smoke literally

14:59:50.603 --> 14:59:54.240
I couldn't see. It was a wall of smoke and if you were in it, you couldn't see. If you were

14:59:55.308 --> 14:59:57.743
were out of it, you could just see the wall of smoke.

14:59:57.743 --> 14:59:58.411
I'm sorry for interrupting.

14:59:58.444 --> 14:59:59.879
How difficult was the evacuation?

15:00:00.046 --> 15:00:02.915
I'm sorry, say that again, Peter?

15:00:03.316 --> 15:00:07.219
How difficult was was it to evacuate the building from? At least from the 30,

15:00:07.219 --> 15:00:09.622
there were 110 stories in the building.

15:00:11.190 --> 15:00:18.230
I would say that it wasn't. It wasn't extremely difficult, it was just slow going down a somewhat narrow stairwell.

15:00:18.297 --> 15:00:24.003
If there was any sort of, you know, people who weren't able to move quickly, then it literally please slow down or.

15:00:24.103 --> 15:00:24.937
Stopped everybody.

15:00:25.871 --> 15:00:31.177
I was on 36, so it wasn't too terrible when I got down to, you know, the 15th or 12th floor or so.

15:00:32.144 --> 15:00:42.455
There was water coming in from the doors, you know, kind of at our feet level, and then it just was a waterfall. Down all of it, continually down all of the stairs. Probably, you know, in some cases, three, four inches deep.

15:00:42.521 --> 15:00:48.194
It's up, sirens and alarms are going off, and then people started to get a little frantic there.

15:00:49.128 --> 15:00:50.129
Dennis, Thank you very much.

15:00:50.329 --> 15:00:50.529
Okay.

15:00:50.529 --> 15:00:52.098
I, I really appreciate you calling in.

15:00:52.164 --> 15:00:52.298
Dr.

15:00:52.531 --> 15:00:52.865
Krause,

15:00:53.332 --> 15:00:53.766
who works...

15:01:09.315 --> 15:01:09.448
I

15:01:09.448 --> 15:01:10.750
was in the first building that was hit.

15:01:11.717 --> 15:01:12.785
It seemed like a plane hit.

15:01:12.785 --> 15:01:13.886
We thought it was an earthquake.

15:01:13.919 --> 15:01:15.287
We were on the 10th floor.

15:01:15.688 --> 15:01:16.856
The whole thing was shaking,

15:01:16.956 --> 15:01:18.190
swaying, like you wouldn't believe.

15:01:18.591 --> 15:01:19.825
Then we all went into the hallways.

15:01:19.825 --> 15:01:20.860
We ran down the stairs.

15:01:20.860 --> 15:01:21.727
A lot of people fell,

15:01:21.727 --> 15:01:22.294
were getting hurt.

15:01:22.661 --> 15:01:23.696
Then when we got out.

15:01:23.763 --> 15:01:24.263
Outside the building,

15:01:24.263 --> 15:01:26.432
the second plane went crashing into the other building.

15:01:26.966 --> 15:01:28.834
And then the whole top of the building just collapsed. now,

15:01:28.868 --> 15:01:29.535
that's what I'm hearing.

15:01:30.936 --> 15:01:33.072
Unbelievable.

15:01:33.072 --> 15:01:33.839
Tony Ciarnella.

15:01:34.874 --> 15:01:36.242
C-I-A-R-N-E-L-L-A.

15:01:36.242 --> 15:01:36.742
How do you do that,

15:01:36.742 --> 15:01:38.044
though?

15:01:38.044 --> 15:01:39.045
I work for Bank of America.

15:01:39.045 --> 15:01:42.782
Can you tell us exactly how you do it?

15:01:42.782 --> 15:01:43.582
That's a good question.

15:01:43.616 --> 15:01:44.283
I really don't know.

15:01:44.283 --> 15:01:44.884
Too far ahead.

15:01:44.884 --> 15:01:45.551
Too far ahead.

15:01:45.584 --> 15:01:46.852
I know we have a contingency site.

15:01:46.852 --> 15:01:47.987
We're probably going to end up there.

15:01:49.555 --> 15:01:50.723
What do you think is the reason you guys are doing this?

15:01:51.957 --> 15:01:53.526
I think that there's some really crazy...

15:01:53.559 --> 15:01:55.227
People in this world.

15:01:55.227 --> 15:01:56.028
This is just not,

15:01:56.829 --> 15:01:57.730
too many innocent people.

15:01:57.763 --> 15:01:59.131
People are jumping off the building,

15:01:59.799 --> 15:02:01.167
body parts all over the place.

15:02:01.200 --> 15:02:01.434
I mean,

15:02:01.434 --> 15:02:01.801
this is just,

15:02:02.168 --> 15:02:03.269
